hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1223","Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Darhami told us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam, he is Ibn Hawshab, Sulayman bin Abi told me Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “My friend advised me to do three things that I will not abandon: not to sleep except after praying the Witr prayer, and not to miss the two rak’ahs of the forenoon prayer.” For it is the prayer of those who repent, and fasting for three days of every month.”"
"1224","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ismail bin Abdullah bin Zurarah Al-Raqi told us in Baghdad, Khaled bin Abdullah told us, and he told me Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one performs the noon prayer except one who is steadfast.” He said: “It is the prayer of those who return.” Abu Bakr said: This Sheikh Ismail bin Abdullah was not followed up on the delivery of this news. It was narrated by Al-Darawardi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, mursal, and it was narrated by Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, who said"
